# Useful Linux Commands from Invitational 3

Commands I used during the competition on kvigindis, Ubuntu 24.04.

## First Things First

```bash
# Change root password immediately
passwd root

# Check who is logged in right now
w

# See recent logins
last -20
```

## Recon

```bash
# List all users with a shell
getent passwd | grep -v nologin | grep -v /bin/false

# Check for UID 0 accounts besides root
getent passwd | awk -F: '$3 == 0 {print}'

# See all listening ports and what process owns them
ss -tlnp

# List running services
systemctl list-units --type=service --state=running

# Check firewall status
ufw status verbose
```

## Hunting Persistence

```bash
# Check for NOPASSWD sudo access
grep -r "NOPASSWD" /etc/sudoers /etc/sudoers.d/ 2>/dev/null

# List all systemd timers
systemctl list-timers --all

# Check for bashrc backdoors
grep -n "useradd\|curl\|wget\|nc \|ncat\|bash -i\|/dev/tcp" /root/.bashrc /home/*/.bashrc 2>/dev/null

# Find hidden SSH key backdoors
find / -name authorized_keys 2>/dev/null
cat /etc/ssh/.ssh/authorized_keys 2>/dev/null

# Check all crontabs
for u in $(cut -d: -f1 /etc/passwd); do
  out=$(crontab -l -u "$u" 2>/dev/null | grep -v "^#" | grep -v "^$")
  [ -n "$out" ] && echo "$u: $out"
done

# Recently modified service files in the last 2 hours
find /etc/systemd/system -name "*.service" -mmin -120 2>/dev/null

# Check for rogue processes
ps aux | grep -vE "root|www-data|systemd|sshd|nginx|docker|wazuh|ossec|dbus|message|syslog|_apt|chrony|nobody|polkitd"
```

## Cleaning Persistence

```bash
# Delete a rogue user and their home directory
userdel -r svc_health

# Remove NOPASSWD sudoers file
rm /etc/sudoers.d/svc_health

# Stop and disable a malicious timer/service
systemctl stop health-check.timer
systemctl disable health-check.timer
systemctl stop health-check.service
systemctl disable health-check.service
rm /etc/systemd/system/health-check.timer
rm /etc/systemd/system/health-check.service
systemctl daemon-reload

# Remove bashrc backdoor lines
cat /root/.bashrc
nano /root/.bashrc

# Remove hidden SSH key directory
rm -rf /etc/ssh/.ssh/
```

## Hardening

```bash
# Set up UFW firewall
ufw default deny incoming
ufw default allow outgoing
ufw allow 22/tcp
ufw allow 80/tcp
ufw allow 443/tcp
ufw allow 9000/tcp
ufw enable

# Fix SSH cert auth to prevent cert forgery
sed -i 's|AuthorizedPrincipalsFile none|AuthorizedPrincipalsFile /etc/ssh/auth_principals/%u|' /etc/ssh/sshd_config
mkdir -p /etc/ssh/auth_principals
# Create a principal file per user
echo "username" > /etc/ssh/auth_principals/username
systemctl restart sshd

# Check PHP dangerous functions are disabled in a container
docker exec <container> php -i | grep disable_functions

# Rotate root password
passwd root
```

